      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory Interstate e-Way Bills, Regulatory Clearances &amp; 100% Marine Insurance for ambernath to pune movers and packers</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When you hire a professional <strong>packers and movers in Ambernath</strong> to relocate your household to Pune, the journey must be backed by a series of statutory transit documents that protect both the cargo and the customer.</p>

<p>The first requirement is the <strong>GST e‑Way bill</strong>. This electronic waybill is issued for every interstate move and guarantees that the goods are legally transported under the Goods and Services Tax framework. Without an e‑Way bill, the shipment can be held up at the border or subjected to penalties.</p>

<p>Next, the carrier must provide an <strong>IBA‑approved Lorry Receipt (LR/Bilty)</strong>. The LR is a formal proof of carriage and includes details such as vehicle number, driver, load weight, and route. It serves as the contract between the mover and the client and is essential for resolving any disputes that may arise during transit.</p>

<p>To cover unforeseen risks, the mover should obtain a <strong>100 % declared‑value IRDAI marine transit insurance</strong>. Though the term “marine” is used for standardization, the policy covers accidental collision, fire, theft, and delays caused by weather or traffic. The full declared value ensures that you are compensated for the complete worth of your belongings.</p>

